    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a9ba9532-cace-5594-b558-e1722519c3b5",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $det(A)=-1$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=7 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=-1$, so $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=7$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $A\\text{ is invertible}$. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true: $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\n- Statement III is false: $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and II only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a174e852-39f1-55a8-9fb0-60d6f5959409",
